{"2309900": {"success": true, "data": {"type": "game", "name": "Shadows Of Deceit", "steam_appid": 2309900, "required_age": 0, "is_free": false, "controller_support": "full", "detailed_description": "<h1>Feature List</h1><p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\"><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2309900/extras/8d43b0cede0f5d6be2cee8c53b661d73.poster.avif?t=1775951214\" width=600 height=170 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2309900/extras/8d43b0cede0f5d6be2cee8c53b661d73.webm?t=1775951214\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2309900/extras/8d43b0cede0f5d6be2cee8c53b661d73.mp4?t=1775951214\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Truth is not written. It is trapped,</strong> relive the same moments again and again. Each loop brings you closer to what really happened.   </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Uncover what happened through fragments of the past that resurface when reality breaks, </strong>an intimate, haunting story told through silence, memory, and the spaces in between.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>A multi-layered narrative thriller</strong>, blending mystery, psychological horror, and temporal dislocation.  </p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>You are not alone</strong>, Something remains in the shadows. Not a single pursuer, but fractured human shapes that surface when you least expect them.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p></p><br><h1>Just Updated</h1><p>At the moment, we are working on full support for the Xbox Controller, which will be available in the final version of Shadows of Deceit.</p><br><h1>About the Game</h1><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2309900/extras/17ae3afab79f8f887d8fae1bbd8a7deb.poster.avif?t=1775951214\" width=600 height=252 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2309900/extras/17ae3afab79f8f887d8fae1bbd8a7deb.webm?t=1775951214\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2309900/extras/17ae3afab79f8f887d8fae1bbd8a7deb.mp4?t=1775951214\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>1999 – HAVENBROOK, UNITED STATES.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Journalist Janet Sheperd returns to her hometown to find a photograph. It's the only recent photo of her best friend, Isabelle Nox, who disappeared two years ago.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A memorial is being prepared. Janet needs that photo.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The photo is hidden somewhere inside her family's old hotel, now abandoned and awaiting demolition. With her is Lucas, a childhood friend, and their old walkie-talkies.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >But as Janet searches through dusty rooms and forgotten corridors, something shifts. Hallways repeat. Time fractures. Events loop. Voice on the walkie-talkie begins to change, saying things he shouldn't know.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >And other places start to bleed through the hotel: a university campus, a hospital, a school. Places where Janet lost something more than a friend. Places where she lost herself.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The deeper she goes, the more the building remembers.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >And so does she.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >To find the photo, Janet must uncover what really happened the night Isabelle vanished. The night her mind chose to forget.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>Some places are abandoned.</i><br><i>Others are waiting.</i></p>", "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2309900/extras/17ae3afab79f8f887d8fae1bbd8a7deb.poster.avif?t=1775951214\" width=600 height=252 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2309900/extras/17ae3afab79f8f887d8fae1bbd8a7deb.webm?t=1775951214\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2309900/extras/17ae3afab79f8f887d8fae1bbd8a7deb.mp4?t=1775951214\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>1999 – HAVENBROOK, UNITED STATES.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Journalist Janet Sheperd returns to her hometown to find a photograph. It's the only recent photo of her best friend, Isabelle Nox, who disappeared two years ago.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A memorial is being prepared. Janet needs that photo.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The photo is hidden somewhere inside her family's old hotel, now abandoned and awaiting demolition. With her is Lucas, a childhood friend, and their old walkie-talkies.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >But as Janet searches through dusty rooms and forgotten corridors, something shifts. Hallways repeat. Time fractures. Events loop. Voice on the walkie-talkie begins to change, saying things he shouldn't know.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >And other places start to bleed through the hotel: a university campus, a hospital, a school. Places where Janet lost something more than a friend. Places where she lost herself.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The deeper she goes, the more the building remembers.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >And so does she.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >To find the photo, Janet must uncover what really happened the night Isabelle vanished. The night her mind chose to forget.</p><p cl